# Line-ending normalization
#
# This repo previously had core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, so on
# Windows Git flagged unchanged files as "modified" whenever a checkout
# touched their mtimes (phantom CRLF / stat-cache churn). The committed blobs
# are already LF; pinning the working tree to LF as well makes line-ending
# handling deterministic and overrides any per-user core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Prettier (no endOfLine override -> default "lf") and the Python/Astro
# toolchain all expect LF, so LF everywhere keeps formatters and Git in sync.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize line endings or attempt text diffs.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
